 "verdict": "partly consistent: the marginal correction supplies a second rāʾ; the pendant sign takes both sīn and shīn in the recorded words.",
 "notes": "The two-area insertion on l.5 is consequential. The main row reads اهجر immediately followed by the ḥāʾ-sign and then the divider and اغـ. There is a small mark above ḥāʾ. Farther left in the margin, beyond اغـ, a divider and the capped hooked rāʾ carry a second small mark. Reading that insertion before the ḥāʾ restores اهجر | رح without adding a spurious letter to اغد across ll.5–6. The transcription places the marginal rāʾ in reading order; the small accompanying reference mark is not counted. On l.6 the first sign of the short disputed pair has the familiar pendant used in اسر and اشف, and the second word begins with the gate with curved foot (خ in خن and اخلص). Reading شر / خر retains the clear record’s uncertain vowels/dots. In اسفل, a V on a bar with loop below differs from the plain pendant. The last two groups are اضلل اخلص.",
 "fit_against_record_wording": "Each of 38 short imperative groups can be aligned including the inserted divider and rāʾ on l.5. The normalization separates adjoining imperatives and reads اجمل and اخلص. The sīn/shīn reading on l.6 remains less secure."
